Helix H.264 encoder: do not redefine MAX and MIN

Linux 6.6 defines MAX() and MIN() in linux/minmax.h, which every file of
the driver includes before h264enc/slice.h. With -Werror the second
definition stops the build. The driver's versions are the same
expressions, so take the kernel's when it has them.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver]

--- a/module_drivers/drivers/media/platform/ingenic-vcodec/helix/h264enc/slice.h
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/media/platform/ingenic-vcodec/helix/h264enc/slice.h
@@ -9,8 +9,12 @@
 	M_SLICE_TYPE_I  = 2,
 };
 
+#ifndef MAX
 #define MAX(X, Y) ((X) >= (Y) ? (X) : (Y))
+#endif
+#ifndef MIN
 #define MIN(X, Y) ((X) <= (Y) ? (X) : (Y))
+#endif
 
 #define QP_MAX_SPEC             (51)
 
